{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped","id":917135,"title":"[Lunars] Characters from other media who felt trapped","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-18T20:34:11-07:00","id":917135,"title":"[Lunars] Characters from other media who felt trapped","content":"Since it seems that Third Edition's Luna chooses her children from those who were willing to sacrifice anything - even their lives - for personal freedom, I think it would be useful to compile a list of such characters from other stories.<br /> <br /> This category <i>is</i> going to overlap with other possible Exalted. The idea is not &quot;only those who were trapped and tried to escape can be Lunars&quot; but rather &quot;Lunars can only be those who were trapped and tried to escape&quot;. It's about who Lunars are rather than what other Exalted are not.<br /> <br /> I would never think of Tony Stark as a Lunar, but his origin story of being held captive by the Ten Rings and risking his life to escape is something that can lead to a Solar Exaltation. (Though one might argue he was less concerned with personal freedom and more with personal responsibilities beyond his imprisonment.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I once composed a list of how the game of <i>Skyrim</i> would play out if the Dragonborn had Exalted. As a Solar or Sidereal, it just happens. He cannot be a Terrestrial without the blood of the dragons, or a modern Alchemical without a Exaltation Core. As an Abyssal, he needs to die by an uninterrupted beheading or because of the dragon; as a classical Alchemical, he actually dies and stays dead a while before being brought back on the slab. A Liminal made from his corpse is someone new.<br /> <br /> Until the corebook came out, I didn't see a particular difference between the Solar and Lunar, but now I do.<br /> <br /> I think Luna <i>doesn't</i> choose the one who decides to give up and die with dignity on the chopping block. <i>I</i> think she chooses the young man who decided to actually try running away, even if it meant getting shot in the back. He breathes in her Second Breath and makes good on his escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:26:51-07:00","id":917159,"title":"","content":"<i>RWBY</i>'s Blake Belladonna. When society discriminates against her because of their racial prejudices, she goes, 'No, fuck YOU' and runs away to become a terrorist. When the terrorists start ordering her to murder innocent people, she goes, 'No, fuck YOU' and runs away to enlist in an army. She cares more about being true to herself than being labelled a traitor and hunted by both sides.<br /> <br /> ...Do I have the right idea? Honestly, I don't understand very much of what OP was saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:31:05-07:00","id":917160,"title":"","content":"Would the Unconquered Sun actually choose the one who decides to give up and die with dignity on the chopping block though? Would the Deathlords/the Underworld, even?<br /> <br /> Perhaps, is it more accurate to say that Luna chooses <i>not</i> those who try to heroically accomplish something and in that moment gain the power to succeed, but those who <i>can</i> and <i>do</i> achieve their freedom regardless of the seeming consequences, which Luna's blessing then empowers them to surpass?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:33:00-07:00","id":917162,"title":"","content":"The closest thing I have seen to a Lunar in Fiction has to be Anyanwu from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Seed_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Octavia Butler's Wild Seed</a>. She has complete control over her body and has to eat a part of an animal to learn how to become it. She even has an Abyssal Mate in Doro, the other immortal character in the novel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:34:47-07:00","id":917163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917159#post917159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>RWBY</i>'s Blake Belladonna. When society discriminates against her because of their racial prejudices, she goes, 'No, fuck YOU' and runs away to become a terrorist. When the terrorists start ordering her to murder innocent people, she goes, 'No, fuck YOU' and runs away to enlist in an army. She cares more about being true to herself than being labelled a traitor and hunted by both sides.<br /> <br /> ...Do I have the right idea? Honestly, I don't understand very much of what OP was saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think you picked a good example.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, Blake didn't go out of her way to become a terrorist. The White Fang was originally a peaceful protest organization. But she DID feel trapped within the terrorist organization that the White Fang became, and threw it all away when she fled.<br /> <br /> One can argue that she fled so that she could pursue her ideal of peaceful and eglitarian coexistence rather than personal freedom, which can be Solar (the Solar Exalted have the Night Caste and can be beast-folk), but it may be close enough. It's definitely close enough for inspiration.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-19-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:36:16-07:00","id":917164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917162#post917162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing I have seen to a Lunar in Fiction has to be Anyanwu from <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Seed_(novel)&amp;quot;]Octavia</a> Butler's Wild Seed[/URL]. She has complete control over her body and has to eat a part of an animal to learn how to become it. She even has an Abyssal Mate in Doro, the other immortal character in the novel.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what does that have to do with this topic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:38:53-07:00","id":917166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917160#post917160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps, is it more accurate to say that Luna chooses <i>not</i> those who try to heroically accomplish something and in that moment gain the power to succeed, but those who <i>can</i> and <i>do</i> achieve their freedom regardless of the seeming consequences, which Luna's blessing then empowers them to surpass?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation is a brutal world. Sometimes people try and fail through no fault of their own.<br /> If only people who don't need Exaltation get it, that erases about half of the possible backstories for a PC. Having conflict in their lives before they can overcome it, not being eternally perfectly capable- that is also part of the hero's journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:42:27-07:00","id":917167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917163#post917163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Blake didn't go out of her way to become a terrorist. The White Fang was originally a peaceful protest organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Implying otherwise kinda devalues her integrity- sorry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917162#post917162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing I have seen to a Lunar in Fiction has to be Anyanwu from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Seed_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Octavia Butler's Wild Seed</a>. She has complete control over her body and has to eat a part of an animal to learn how to become it. She even has an Abyssal Mate in Doro, the other immortal character in the novel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds more relevant <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here\">to another thread</a>. This debate is about 3E Lunars, specifically, and examining the philosophy behind their Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 06-19-2016, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:43:30-07:00","id":917169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917164#post917164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what does that have to do with this topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyanwu is trapped in a relationship with Doro, another Immortal being with the ability to steal bodies. He forces her to bear children for him as part of his breeding program to create a race of supernatural humans. She escapes him by fleeing in animal form. (He can not take her body while she is an animal) One if the major themes of the book how much power can an individual have over someone. Doro totally dominates his people, kills them for thier bodies, and because he raised them, they love him for it. Anyanwu rejects Doro's control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:44:23-07:00","id":917171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917160#post917160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Unconquered Sun actually choose the one who decides to give up and die with dignity on the chopping block though? Would the Deathlords/the Underworld, even?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sun would when, in response to the dragon attack, the character decides to fight the dragon to save the town.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps, is it more accurate to say that Luna chooses... those who <i>can</i> and <i>do</i> achieve their freedom regardless of the seeming consequences, which Luna's blessing then empowers them to surpass? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Achieving their freedom&quot; is a meaningless distinction point. Luna ought to choose those who try, and they succeed with her power whether they needed it or not.<br /> <br /> She canonically Exalted a woman who threw herself into the sea to be eaten by sharks, rather than become a sex slave. How &quot;free&quot; would that woman have been, and for how long? Luna rebirthed her on the spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T21:45:21-07:00","id":917173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917167#post917167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds more relevant <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/11921-the-great-marriage-of-exalted-and-insert-fandom-here&amp;quot;]to</a> another thread[/URL]. This debate is about 3E Lunars, specifically, and examining the philosophy behind their Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. I misunderstood the purpose of this topic. <br /> <br /> Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:11:48-07:00","id":917184,"title":"","content":"Edmond Dantes may have too many Abyssal motifs- someone in-universe literally describes him as a vampire- but his tradition from 'Skilled yet unambitious ship captain' to 'Vengeful aristocratic renaissance man' seems relevant to this thread nonetheless. The transition comes when he disguises himself as a dead body in order to escape prison, and somehow manages to survive being thrown off a cliff, into freezing cold water, in the middle of the night, after being trapped and tortured for several years. Then he swims several miles until finding a ship that takes him onboard.<br /> (Yes, it's that kind of story.)<br /> Anyway, he attributes his survival to God supporting him and goes on to believe that this means God wants him to take revenge- a jump in logic pretty applicable to many Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:12:54-07:00","id":917185,"title":"","content":"Reposting from here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/780189-first-character-of-a-specific-splat-planned-3e-musings\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ned-3e-musings</a><br /> <br /> Ever since I learned about the Lunar's new &quot;Chosen for breaking their chains&quot; narrative, I had this idea.<br /> <br /> A princess (mortal or Dragon-Blood) is given a male slave taken from an oppressed local people-group. In actuality, he was chosen and trained by elements within his people with the <i>intent</i> that he become a slave in the castle to act as an inside agent and eventual assassin.<br /> <br /> When the day comes that they finally storm the castle, the slave has decided to break free and make his own destiny. He Exalts as a Lunar and slaughters absolutely every one of... his own people.<br /> <br /> He had grown to love the princess, and had felt trapped by the duties imposed upon him by his own people. He rejected slavery to his past and continues to build his own place and destiny as the secret protector of the woman he loves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:28:16-07:00","id":917189,"title":"","content":"He's kind of a robot and all, but Blade Wolf's backtory (I think it's DLC) in Metal Gear Revengeance is all about this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mp83nleLe2I\" data-code=\"mp83nleLe2I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/mp83nleLe2I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> His theme song, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XgCZixSjVX0\" data-code=\"XgCZixSjVX0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XgCZixSjVX0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>I'm My Own Master Now</b><br /> <br /> Born<br /> Into a pack<br /> There\u2019s no choice<br /> But take orders to attack<br /> <br /> Locked up in chains<br /> I get fed<br /> But the hunger still remains<br /> <br /> Not content to live this way<br /> Being led by the blind<br /> Got to plan my dispersal<br /> Time to leave them all behind<br /> <br /> Breaking out of my pain<br /> Nothing ventured \u2013 nothing gained<br /> I\u2019m my own master now<br /> <br /> Bear the mark of my scars<br /> Shedding blood underneath the stars<br /> But I will survive somehow<br /> <br /> Oooooooo<br /> Oooooooo<br /> <br /> Hear me howl<br /> Time to leave them all behind<br /> I\u2019m my own master now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-21-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:32:11-07:00","id":917367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917166#post917166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation is a brutal world. Sometimes people try and fail through no fault of their own.<br /> If only people who don't need Exaltation get it, that erases about half of the possible backstories for a PC. Having conflict in their lives before they can overcome it, not being eternally perfectly capable- that is also part of the hero's journey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation is a brutal world, and not all those who might become divine heroes do so. But whether they succeed or fail through circumstances out of their control or their own lacking, their actions have value. That is one reason why the Sun and Moon take notice to begin with. But I was speaking specifically to the difference between solar and lunar exaltation.<br /> <br /> That said you're right, it's not a desirable narrowing of backstory elements. &quot;Achieve&quot; was poor choice of words on my part, as it reduces the role of freedom in becoming a Lunar to a degree of resolution that may be altogether more suited to the narrative of <i>being</i> a Lunar and what Luna's Chosen seek with their power, if their Ex3 spoof is anything to go by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917171#post917171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sun would when, in response to the dragon attack, the character decides to fight the dragon to save the town.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but then we're not necessarily talking about the Dragonborn anymore. (Nor &quot;accepting your execution with dignity&quot; in a vacuum, but in hindsight that's not a logical assumption to make when speaking of an exalt's Second Breath anyway.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917171#post917171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Achieving their freedom&quot; is a meaningless distinction point. Luna ought to choose those who try, and they succeed with her power whether they needed it or not.<br /> <br /> She canonically Exalted a woman who threw herself into the sea to be eaten by sharks, rather than become a sex slave. How &quot;free&quot; would that woman have been, and for how long? Luna rebirthed her on the spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Questioning that distinction was exactly my intent, because as said, there is overlap with the circumstances of the other Exalted, and interest in determining where there isn't.<br /> <br /> I took that into account when I mentioned &quot;regardless of the seeming consequences&quot;, but as aforementioned I could have expressed myself better. &quot;Luna chooses those who take freedom over bondage, no matter what that freedom might entail&quot; is better, and you certainly can't say that canonical character didn't take the chance to escape a destiny of slavery when she could, even if it would've meant death without Luna's intervention.<br /> <br /> I think there's a space where we can distinguish 'simply' trying for freedom and picking freedom no matter what, with the reasons why Luna is drawn to her chosen falling in the latter, but it's admittedly an ambiguous difference.<br /> <br /> That is what my reading of the limited Lunar material in third edition tells me, anyhow. But this is likely derailing into a discussion for another thread, so I apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-19-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:57:35-07:00","id":917437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917367#post917367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, but then we're not necessarily talking about the Dragonborn anymore. (Nor &quot;accepting your execution with dignity&quot; in a vacuum, but in hindsight that's not a logical assumption to make when speaking of an exalt's Second Breath anyway.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was heavily abridging my original Skyrim scenario. I still am. <br /> <br /> For a Solar Exaltation, the player character who went to the chopping block, upon having his execution canceled because of Sudden Dragon Attack, decides to do something about the dragon to protect the village, or at least to evacuate the people. The Sun chooses him for choosing to try and make a difference in the world rather than concentrate on his own life. The Sun gives him the power to make that difference.<br /> <br /> Luna doesn't care; those actions don't inspire her. She wants someone who would choose to live or even die on his own terms, without regard for dignity. She doesn't care if, after surviving the arrow and escaping the guards, her new Lunar child sees the dragon and turns around to save the village. That is her Chosen's choice, which she gave him the freedom to choose. <br /> <br /> The Moon is not the Sun. Let the Sun choose the character given to the player. The Moon wants the young man who ran.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's a space where we can distinguish 'simply' trying for freedom and picking freedom no matter what, with the reasons why Luna is drawn to her chosen falling in the latter, but it's admittedly an ambiguous difference. </div> </div> </div>You will definitely need to explain yourself better, but I am not seeing what you are driving at. <br /> <br /> Distinguishing this matter seems very relevant to the thread, not a derail.<br /> <br /> At least, so long as people keep trying to name various kinds of slaves who risked everything for any kind of freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:25:48-07:00","id":917461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917160#post917160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Unconquered Sun actually choose the one who decides to give up and die with dignity on the chopping block though? Would the Deathlords/the Underworld, even?<br /> <br /> Perhaps, is it more accurate to say that Luna chooses <i>not</i> those who try to heroically accomplish something and in that moment gain the power to succeed, but those who <i>can</i> and <i>do</i> achieve their freedom regardless of the seeming consequences, which Luna's blessing then empowers them to surpass?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sol would empower the guy leading the rebellion <i>while he was leading the rebellion</i> if he were going to do so at all. If he doesn't, and the rebellion fails and that guy gets captured, yeah, he might very well stoically march to the gallows and die with dignity, vowing with his last breath that his people would someday be free (he was a Solar candidate, after all; one expects a certain amount of unreasonable pride). Had he tried to slip his bonds and make a break for it against all odds to fight another day, in that moment Luna might take notice and Exalt him.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading Sunder correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:14:17-07:00","id":917486,"title":"","content":"I thought continuing to challenge/discuss the premise rather than contributing would be derailing, but I suppose it's important. I know what the distinction means to me, but I find it difficult to explain with a magnitude of appreciable clarity, and I'm feeling like my basis for it may be somewhat mistaken anyways, so I'm just going to mull on it for a while and try to remember examples of Lunars where the main topic is concerned.<br /> <br /> @Blackwell: Hmm, I guess that sounds right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:23:42-07:00","id":917490,"title":"","content":"I think something that would go along with the Lunar concept of breaking their chains is that they're still supposed to be outsiders and iconoclasts. People who are apart, and heavily constrained by convention, who finally have a cathartic moment of seeking or breaking away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T12:35:12-07:00","id":917497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917461#post917461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Sol would empower the guy leading the rebellion <i>while he was leading the rebellion</i> if he were going to do so at all. If he doesn't, and the rebellion fails and that guy gets captured, yeah, he might very well stoically march to the gallows and die with dignity, vowing with his last breath that his people would someday be free (he was a Solar candidate, after all; one expects a certain amount of unreasonable pride). Had he tried to slip his bonds and make a break for it against all odds to fight another day, in that moment Luna might take notice and Exalt him.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading Sunder correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because I'm talking about the player character of the game, not Ulfric Stormcloak. And I'm not talking about leading the rebellion last week, I'm talking about leading the people at hand in order to do something about the dragon burning the village down right now.<br /> <br /> In the game, all you can do is escape the dragon rather than fight, because that is all that is scripted and Exaltations aren't a thing that can happen.<br /> <br /> But in Creation, outside of a scripted game, the player character can obviously choose to step up and fight the dragon or organize an escape, and thereby be chosen by the Sun.<br /> <br /> But he would not be chosen by Luna, who was watching the moments in which the player character could choose to submit or die free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:45:32-07:00","id":917660,"title":"","content":"Riddick certainly fits the &quot;freedom at any cost&quot; theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T19:55:06-07:00","id":917742,"title":"","content":"From my lost-but-recorded &quot;...and then he became an oni&quot; thread...<br /> <br /> <br /> There were once two children lost in a forest, and they fell into a Fair Folk's candied trap.<br /> <br /> The faerie caged the brother and made the sister to help her in fattening him up, that the monster might eat him. Not that the monster desired his flesh, but rather lusted for the despair and horror of the sibling to be eaten and the sibling made to betray.<br /> <br /> But the monster underestimated the siblings' ingenuity. They quickly learned how to divide their hearts, that they might outwardly seem broken while inwardly observing and plotting.<br /> <br /> Behind the witch's back, they even learned to pick the lock of the cage, but with no chance to escape they instead used the opportunity to trade clothing and places, that the sister might likewise receive the strengthening meals and the brother might exercise his body.<br /> <br /> In the moment of truth, the elf had no warning, surprised by the siblings' sudden ferocity and combined might. They threw her into the blazing oven, and held the door shut as she burned to death, roasted as much by their hatred as the faerie-fire.<br /> <br /> In savage vengeance, they ate HER gossamer flesh, stealing her power for their own before likewise plundering her belongings.<br /> <br /> Now they set out for home, to reunite with their father... and make their step-mother <i>pay</i>.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-20-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T20:05:54-07:00","id":917746,"title":"","content":"The Japanese have a fairy tale called, &quot;The Boy Who Drew Cats&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> A farmer and his wife had many children; the youngest son was too small and weak, and spent all his time drawing cats instead of doing his chores. So, they took him to the temple to become a priest. He learned quickly, but continued to draw cats everywhere with his calligraphy brush.<br /> <br /> The old priest marveled at the skill with which he painted the cats; it seemed as though they might leap off the paper at any moment! But this could not be allowed to continue. The old priest delivered his ultimatum: either the boy must finally cease all painting and devote himself only to his studies, or he must leave the temple to see if he could survive in the world as an artist.<br /> <br /> The boy chose his freedom.<br /> <br /> On his way to town, he spotted a large, abandoned building - a temple with paper walls, such as he had grown up within. Seized by a childhood desire long suppressed, he made his way to the temple and drew cats across every paper surface, floor to ceiling in all of the rooms. Eventually, night fell, and he found a secure place to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> Unbeknownst to him, who spent so much time painting that he paid so little attention to gossip, this temple had been abandoned because a goblin-rat had invaded and made its home there, driving the priests away. Exorcists and warriors who came to kill it were never seen again.<br /> <br /> That night, the young man dreamt of a gigantic, angry rat that meant to tear him apart for the affront of painting his home with cats, but a swarm of cats leapt upon him and tore him apart.<br /> <br /> When the young man awoke, he was shocked to see all of his painted cats grinning down at him with mouths wet and red from blood, and the floor spotted with bloody paw prints, with gouges all over as if carved by massive claws.<br /> <br /> Then he found the corpse of the enormous goblin-rat, ripped to pieces.<br /> <br /> The boy went on to become a famous painter who only drew cats, and the city where he dwelt never feared for vermin or bandits or monsters again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T20:48:54-07:00","id":917759,"title":"","content":"Feeling trapped, I kind of like the idea of feeling trapped like an animal and animal instinct taking over for some lunar exaltation...of course I could be totally wrong in my interpretation:<br /> <br /> Gohan SSJ2 transformation vs Cell:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XebyKpo6A9s\" data-code=\"XebyKpo6A9s\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XebyKpo6A9s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Gon's rage over his loss:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qb5Z8E0MoLY\" data-code=\"qb5Z8E0MoLY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qb5Z8E0MoLY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Eren transformation (I guess spoilers but whatever):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GLff3_jPZIM\" data-code=\"GLff3_jPZIM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GLff3_jPZIM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:59:00-07:00","id":918091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917490#post917490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something that would go along with the Lunar concept of breaking their chains is that they're still supposed to be outsiders and iconoclasts. People who are apart, and heavily constrained by convention, who finally have a cathartic moment of seeking or breaking away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> There was no indication that shark lady was either an iconoclast or an outsider within her native culture. She broke the chains of a <i>foreign</i> culture.<br /> <br /> You would be correct for Lunars who felt trapped by their own cultures, but that is clearly not the case for the Lunar Exalted as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:50:58-07:00","id":918312,"title":"","content":"I've seen a few people suggest Morgiana of <i>Magi </i>as a Lunar Exalt. Sadly, she wouldn't seem to meet these criteria because she did not seek to escape her captivity from Jamil on her own.<br /> <br /> At least, not on-screen. It's possible that Morgiana once attempted to escape, failed, and was <i>not </i>killed or crippled in punishment. In world where Lunar Exaltation is possible, she might have taken the Second Breath. But then, she wouldn't be the same woman we meet in the first episode.<br /> <br /> The Morgiana first seen on-screen is broken in spirit and doesn't dare to even think about taking her freedom. She only gets her freedom because of the actions of others.<br /> <br /> <br /> She's later taken prisoner again, and has <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TejVuMCQmgU\" target=\"_blank\">an Exaltation moment when she frees herself</a>, but this time she's trying to break her bonds in order to save someone else rather than secure her own freedom. Also, the moment is punctuated by a shining savior figure back-lit by the Sun itself telling her that she is no longer a slave. So, I'm thinking she became a Solar Exalt and received a vision from the Unconquered Sun when he Chose her.<br /> <br /> Even ignoring the solar imagery, I repeat that she broke her chains for the sake of someone else rather than for her personal freedom. She sought the power to make a difference in the world according to her new vision of the world, and the Sun chooses to grant his power to people with the vision to use it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any objections?<br /> <br /> <br /> (Even though it has all the trappings of an Exaltation moment, Morgiana doesn't actually become any stronger than she was before. She simply sheds all of her old fear and stops holding herself back.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:30:12-07:00","id":918337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918091#post918091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was no indication that shark lady was either an iconoclast or an outsider within her native culture. She broke the chains of a <i>foreign</i> culture.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat's a good point for not being a case of strictly iconoclasts and outsiders.<br /> <br /> Although... she's said to have been a Chiaroscuran woman taken by debt-slavers. I mean, the actual people trading her were from the Realm, but Chiaroscuro itself still practices slavery, so it would seem to suggest she was somebody being transported as a matter of the debt of herself or somebody else, so there's still an element of being bound by your own society, even if that society proceeds to trade you to somebody else.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think the manner in which that one was written up contains two features that still distinguish it from a general narrative of trying to escape captivity. The one is the matter of being moved for a life of bonded service; not just being imprisoned, but a scenario in which life becomes defined by being owned by somebody.<br /> <br /> The other is the fairly extreme standard to which she would pursue freedom, throwing herself to death rather than living as somebody's toy.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it's reading too much into it to speculate on the nature and significance of her debt... probably. Regular people have debts, some people get enslaved for their debt; I think I actually prefer the idea that she was a conventional person until faced with the possibility of becoming a slave. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:23:20-07:00","id":918400,"title":"","content":"One day, a Lunar Exalt wakes up, and realizes that he doesn't know anything about himself, not even his own name.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, either Luna or a note he wrote to himself explains. He used to be someone who hated himself and what he had done so much that he committed a form of suicide in erasing all of his memories. The note's final words challenge him to live a better life.<br /> <br /> Luna explains that she Chose him for the courage to shed his past so completely. Also because her Gift might be the only thing that will help him survive the immediate future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T03:22:32-07:00","id":918526,"title":"","content":"Depending on circumstances, that sounds like a terrible idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean, suppose the person hated himself for having uncontrolled violent impulses, and wanted to forget doing something really terrible.<br /> <br /> But with no memory, the first new time he experiences a violent impulse, it will come as so much of a shock that he cannot restrain himself, and so proceeds to do something terrible.<br /> <br /> Or if a person hated himself for having experienced continuous failure on account of a bad habit of procrastination, that he suddenly lost the ability to learn from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T05:37:47-07:00","id":918571,"title":"","content":"I can't believe no one has mentioned Arya Stark yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:02:43-07:00","id":918580,"title":"","content":"I'd say this scene qualifies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLrOPV2Z0uM\" data-code=\"dLrOPV2Z0uM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/dLrOPV2Z0uM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:26:50-07:00","id":918590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918580#post918580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say this scene qualifies.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you didn't read post #26?<br /> <br /> Please, do so and respond to my arguments.<br /> <br /> ...Also, it's curious that the version you chose completely cut out the solar vision I mention. Why would the video-poster do that?<br /> <br /> Here is the version I watched, with the scene in question at <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TejVuMCQmgU?t=54\" target=\"_blank\">0:54</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TejVuMCQmgU?t=54\" data-code=\"TejVuMCQmgU\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TejVuMCQmgU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918571#post918571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe no one has mentioned Arya Stark yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to believe that not everyone likes the shows you like. So lots of people haven't made the time to read or watch Game of Thrones.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it would be nice if you explained why you think one of Arya Stark's decisions fits the new ideas of Lunar Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-21-2016, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:49:27-07:00","id":918602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917660#post917660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riddick certainly fits the &quot;freedom at any cost&quot; theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was Thinking that. He's an expert Survivialist who likely Exalted at a very young age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T07:16:55-07:00","id":918608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918526#post918526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on circumstances, that sounds like a terrible idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean, suppose the person hated himself for having uncontrolled violent impulses, and wanted to forget doing something really terrible.<br /> <br /> But with no memory, the first new time he experiences a violent impulse, it will come as so much of a shock that he cannot restrain himself, and so proceeds to do something terrible.<br /> <br /> Or if a person hated himself for having experienced continuous failure on account of a bad habit of procrastination, that he suddenly lost the ability to learn from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That's one reason why so many 'redemption' arcs fail... Contrition <i>in the present moment </i>is important, but if a villain hasn't learned constructive/harmless coping methods along with it, there's nothing to stop them from reacting badly the next time emotion overwhelms them, as emotion overwhelms <i>every</i> human sometimes.<br /> I do agree Sunder's idea is good, though. <i>Glories</i> actually had a really cool thaumaturgy ritual for just that scenario, for a good person who's been forced to do or see terrible things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 06-21-2016, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T07:28:11-07:00","id":918614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918590#post918590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need to believe that not everyone likes the shows you like. So lots of people haven't made the time to read or watch Game of Thrones.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it would be nice if you explained why you think one of Arya Stark's decisions fits the new ideas of Lunar Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more surprise than literal disbelief.<br /> <br /> As to how Arya fits the idea of Lunar Exaltation- she's consistently rebelled against the constraints placed on her by society, violating several social norms (befriending people below her station, disguising herself as a boy, taking an overt pleasure in committing violence upon those she sees as deserving) at first because she wants to, and then in order to survive.<br /> <br /> Spoiler for Game of Thrones season 6, episode 8 &quot;No One&quot;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Her departure from the House of Black and White- her ultimate refusal to surrender her identity and destiny to the Faceless Men, would probably be the pivotal moment that I'd use as her Exaltation as a Lunar, myself.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now, granted, you can also make a case for her being a Solar. I daresay many Lunar Exaltations could be Solar, and many action-oriented Solar Exaltations could be Lunar (on the grounds that the heroic activity is often taken in the service of freedom for oneself or others).<br /> <br /> But, to me, Arya's overriding motivation/theme of 'survive and maintain my agency and autonomy' strike me as profoundly Lunar, both 2e and 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T07:48:03-07:00","id":918621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918590#post918590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you didn't read post #26?<br /> <br /> Please, do so and respond to my arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed that, I will do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918312#post918312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen a few people suggest Morgiana of <i>Magi </i>as a Lunar Exalt. Sadly, she wouldn't seem to meet these criteria because she did not seek to escape her captivity from Jamil on her own.<br /> <br /> At least, not on-screen. It's possible that Morgiana once attempted to escape, failed, and was <i>not </i>killed or crippled in punishment. In world where Lunar Exaltation is possible, she might have taken the Second Breath. But then, she wouldn't be the same woman we meet in the first episode.<br /> <br /> The Morgiana first seen on-screen is broken in spirit and doesn't dare to even think about taking her freedom. She only gets her freedom because of the actions of others.<br /> <br /> She's later taken prisoner again, and has <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TejVuMCQmgU\" target=\"_blank\">an Exaltation moment when she frees herself</a>, but this time she's trying to break her bonds in order to save someone else rather than secure her own freedom. Also, the moment is punctuated by a shining savior figure back-lit by the Sun itself telling her that she is no longer a slave. So, I'm thinking she became a Solar Exalt and received a vision from the Unconquered Sun when he Chose her.<br /> <br /> Even ignoring the solar imagery, I repeat that she broke her chains for the sake of someone else rather than for her personal freedom. She sought the power to make a difference in the world according to her new vision of the world, and the Sun chooses to grant his power to people with the vision to use it.<br /> <br /> Any objections?<br /> <br /> (Even though it has all the trappings of an Exaltation moment, Morgiana doesn't actually become any stronger than she was before. She simply sheds all of her old fear and stops holding herself back.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Morgiana's vision isn't of anything analogous to UCS, it's a memory of a fellow former slave who urged her to free herself.<br /> <br /> In the manga (and presumably later in the anime when it catches up), Morgiana's people are shown to be far more Lunar like. Avoiding spoilers, but the analogue is pretty strong.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's really relevant that she broke her chains to save someone else, she achieved personal freedom regardless. It's the start of a major shift in her character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918590#post918590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Also, it's curious that the version you chose completely cut out the solar vision I mention. Why would the video-poster do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the video was edited to focus on the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-21-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:54:26-07:00","id":918790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918608#post918608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. That's one reason why so many 'redemption' arcs fail... Contrition <i>in the present moment </i>is important, but if a villain hasn't learned constructive/harmless coping methods along with it, there's nothing to stop them from reacting badly the next time emotion overwhelms them, as emotion overwhelms <i>every</i> human sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just about being overwhelmed by emotion; it's a matter of habits, patterns of cognition. The things that you think, the ways that you react that are just the default of you.<br /> <br /> It's similar to muscle memory, and so why people with amnesia can still sign their names, or even sometimes play instruments; there's conditioning in the biological mechanisms.<br /> <br /> A contrite person will at least try to catch themselves in the middle of or after a response they don't like; really changing yourself is a matter of gradually conditioning yourself in another direction.<br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T16:44:34-07:00","id":918848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918621#post918621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morgiana's vision isn't of anything analogous to UCS, it's a memory of a fellow former slave who urged her to free herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know who he is. I did watch at least that many episodes.<br /> <br /> I'm saying that the vision of him could have been the Sun using his appearance. Assuming the face and voice the man that Morgiana considered her savior, since he was acting as her savior now in Choosing her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the manga (and presumably later in the anime when it catches up), Morgiana's people are shown to be far more Lunar like. Avoiding spoilers, but the analogue is pretty strong. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I looked that up.<br /> <br /> But none of that matters as regards this moment. This moment would be largely unchanged if her people happened to have Laser Eyes and Morgiana's major restraint was an eye-blinder that she found a way to smash apart.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think it's really relevant that she broke her chains to save someone else, she achieved personal freedom regardless. </div> </div> </div>But freedom wasn't her goal. Justice, protection, and compassion were her goals. She wanted to make a difference in the world. Such things draw the Sun's attention and approval.<br /> <br /> Morgiana missed out on her chance to earn Luna's approval when she failed to even attempt freeing herself (without or with the girl) before the girl's life was in danger, and even earlier than that when she refused to try escaping Jamil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:53:34-07:00","id":918883,"title":"","content":"Hm...<br /> Jekyll wants to be free of his moral restraints (book) or his evil nature (musical), which might be a bit to abstract, but still freedom.<br /> <br /> Dracula in some versions want's to escape death or the Sultan, plus can turn into a bat or wolf, and commands animals. Archetype for Lunar foil maybe, or a lunar of the underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T19:59:43-07:00","id":918923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918883#post918883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...<br /> Jekyll wants to be free of his moral restraints (book) or his evil nature (musical), which might be a bit to abstract, but still freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is a product of its times, so one reading could be that Jekyll wants to be free of social persecution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dracula in some versions want's to escape death or the Sultan, plus can turn into a bat or wolf, and commands animals. Archetype for Lunar foil maybe, or a lunar of the underworld? </div> </div> </div>Well, Dracula III wasn't associated with vampires until Bram Stoker arbitrarily decided to make him a scary undead foreigner out to corrupt proper English women. Or rather, prior to that, to the Romanians, he was a <i>slayer of vampires</i> for kicking out people who were seen as getting wealthy at the country's expense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-21-2016, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T20:52:25-07:00","id":919489,"title":"","content":"Train Heartnet of <i>Black Cat</i> is very thoroughly a Solar Exalt <i>in aesthetics</i>, but he can be used as inspiration for as a Lunar.<br /> <br /> His backstory is that he was the thirteenth member of the Chronos Numbers, the special enforcers and assassins of the Chronos Organization. Train was especially talented and skilled at assassin -- enough so to be one of the most successful of the Numbers despite lacking any of their passionate loyalty for the organization. He went about his job mechanically, unable to imagine any other life even as he died a little more inside each day.<br /> <br /> One day, he met a bounty hunter full of compassion and carefree joy. Inspired and challenged by her example, Train worked with her to capture bounties without killing them. Train began to imagine a life of a freedom as a bounty hunter who could choose where he went, who he hunted, and whether or not he killed.<br /> <br /> Then one of his creepy admirers, horrified by Train's change of heart, murdered Train's new friend and mentor. That was the last straw for the 13th Number; he killed the murderer (or so he thought), announced his defection, and fought every loyalist assassin who took affront at his treachery. None of the other Numbers stepped in to stop him or those who attacked him, so Train walked away a free man.<br /> <br /> Now Train makes a meager, hand-to-mouth living as a bounty hunter, letting whim and whimsy direct his every choice and action, going anywhere and doing anything simply because it makes him feel alive.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-23-2016, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T06:29:04-07:00","id":923812,"title":"","content":"What you own, owns you.<br /> <br /> The more you own, the more you have to fear losing.<br /> <br /> Rich men live in constant fear of losing their fortunes -- to tax collectors, to foreign conquerors, to thieves, to gold-digging lovers, to impatient heirs, to fire and other natural disasters. The larger their wealth, the more that other people scheme to take it, and the more difficult it is to defend. Often the greed of rich men is enriched by their simple paranoia -- the more wealth they can accumulate, the more they can shore themselves up against potential losses and the better they can recover. But this only creates a vicious cycle, as increasing their wealth only makes it harder to defend and more tempting to steal.<br /> <br /> Few rich men truly admit this trap to themselves. Fewer still admit that it is making them miserable.<br /> <br /> Luna Chose one of the rare-as-hen's-teeth men who had the strength to simply walk away from it all. He gave away all he had, paying back all of his debts and giving the rest away to various loved ones and worthy causes, and requested to join the local Immaculate monastery so that he might find freedom in spiritual enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Becoming one of the Anathema turned that plan on its head, but learning the truth of the world set him freer than he could have imagined.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Luna probably Exalts no few number of heroes who kick an addiction, such as to drugs or alcohol or more unspeakable or exotic things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:23:16-07:00","id":924209,"title":"","content":"Do you know what it is like to feel trapped within your own body, since the day you were born?<br /> <br /> You have never known the vigor or vitality of your friends and neighbors. You tire quickly, injure easily, heal slowly, and catch every seasonal illness. Every time a real sickness starts to spread through town, you must lock yourself away for fear that if you fall under it, you will never wake again.<br /> <br /> You are cursed with the congenital disease of pale blood; if pricked, you bleed, but not crimson red. Your essence is a vague, pearly-grey; watery and thin. This public knowledge, the deathly pallor of your skin, and your frequent bouts of infection have ensured that you grew up a pariah within your community; a figure of pity, scorn, and fear. No one would miss you.<br /> <br /> As an adult, the day came that you could bear your life no more. So one night, with the full moon high in the sky to light your way, you traveled alone through the wilderness, braving brigand and beast, to seek out the infamous, dangerously xenophobic city of Yharnam.<br /> <br /> Few who dared venture to that mad city ever returned, and none with their miracle cure-all. The Yharnamites were as notorious for their stingy control of Blood Ministration as they were for the rumors of monsters lurking in their woods and sewers.<br /> <br /> Under the cover of night, you managed to avoid the beasts and the hunting mobs long enough to find the one man in the whole city who could be begged or bartered into treating your illness. Your hope begins to rise when he recognizes your condition.<br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nbH9jh5zU08\" target=\"_blank\">Ah, yes. Paleblood. </a>Well, you've come to the right place. Yharnam is the home of blood ministration. You need only unravel its mystery. But where's an outsider like yourself to begin? Easy, with a bit of Yharnam blood of your own. But first, you'll need a contract.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nothing about this seems on the level, especially when the blindfolded blood minister insists that you be fully bound to the sick bed for the procedure. But you would rather die than live another day as you are; even the slimmest possibility of freedom is too sweet to refuse. Resolving that any risk is worth it, you accept the contract, lie down, and reign in your panic as the old man straps you down and sticks the needles into your arms.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Moon\" target=\"_blank\">Moon</a> <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Eye\" target=\"_blank\">watches</a> it all, and <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Hunter%27s+Mark\" target=\"_blank\">Chooses</a>.<br /> <br /> As the Yharnam blood begins coursing through your veins, you fall unconscious, and dream feverishly.<br /> <br /> A growing pool of blood, in the richest crimson hue you have ever seen. You can scarcely begin to covet the color before a monster rises up out of it; a wolfish Beast which seems made of <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Impurity\" target=\"_blank\">sticky, hardened, clotted blood</a>. Just looking it seems to remind you of <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Beast\" target=\"_blank\">everything dark and base and nasty about your fellow Man</a>.<br /> <br /> The Beast growls languidly as it approaches you, taking its time as if to <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Blood+Rapture\" target=\"_blank\">draw out the pleasure of your fear</a>. <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Beast%27s+Embrace\" target=\"_blank\">It reaches out to your face</a> with a <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Clawmark\" target=\"_blank\">claw, but turned backwards, as if to brush your cheek in a horrid parody of a woman's alluring invitation</a>.<br /> <br /> At the moment of contact, your Essence sets the Beast <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Radiance\" target=\"_blank\">on fire</a>. The <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Corruption\" target=\"_blank\">tempting sickness</a> it represents is helpless to overcome or withstand <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Heir\" target=\"_blank\">the Lunar Essence which imbued you first</a>, and so the Beast collapses and dies in flames.<br /> <br /> Then you hear a woman's voice, <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Guidance\" target=\"_blank\">kind and gentle</a>. &quot;It seems <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Formless+Oedon\" target=\"_blank\">I</a> have found <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Oedon+Writhe\" target=\"_blank\">myself</a> a <a href=\"http://bloodborne.wiki.fextralife.com/Hunter\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JL5acskAT_2t062HILImBkV8eXAwaqOj611mSjK-vZ8/preview\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...jK-vZ8/preview</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-07-2016, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:04:30-07:00","id":924217,"title":"","content":"Hmm, if I extend the concept of chains to be broken to a life situation that, at first blush, is crushingly inescapable...<br /> <br /> \u200bI wonder at the idea of a Stanley Krelboyne who discovers the ravenous monster inside of his own soul rather than in a Chinese-owned shop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:13:36-07:00","id":924222,"title":"","content":"One thing I find myself coming back to on this subject...<br /> <br /> Many of the characters I think of who felt trapped by other people or in hopeless situations end up choosing to commit suicide (or tried to) as a method of escaping. Would Luna find that action, the cold decision to end ones life rather than live trapped courageous and bless someone with Exaltation and bless them just before they took their own life, or would she view them trying to commit suicide as a way to escape from a painful reality to be weakness and pass them over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:18:34-07:00","id":924224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924217#post924217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, if I extend the concept of chains to be broken to a life situation that, at first blush, is crushingly inescapable...<br /> <br /> \u200bI wonder at the idea of a Stanley Krelboyne who discovers the ravenous monster inside of his own soul rather than in a Chinese-owned shop.</div> </div> </div> </div>A search for that name only turns up a book that cannot be shown, and <i>Malcom in the Middle</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:20:28-07:00","id":924227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924222#post924222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I find myself coming back to on this subject...<br /> <br /> Many of the characters I think of who felt trapped by other people or in hopeless situations end up choosing to commit suicide (or tried to) as a method of escaping. Would Luna find that action, the cold decision to end ones life rather than live trapped courageous and bless someone with Exaltation and bless them just before they took their own life, or would she view them trying to commit suicide as a way to escape from a painful reality to be weakness and pass them over?</div> </div> </div> </div>I once again point out that Luna canonically Exalted a woman who jumped into shark infested waters to die rather than become a sex slave.<br /> <br /> Luna seems to reward those who value freedom more than life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:21:54-07:00","id":924228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924224#post924224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A search for that name only turns up a book that cannot be shown, and <i>Malcom in the Middle</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm taking a wild guess that Isator meant Seymour Krelborn from Little Shop of Horrors as he acquired Audrey 2 in an old chinese shop. That's the closest thing I can think of anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:28:57-07:00","id":924235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=918608#post918608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree Sunder's idea is good, though. <i>Glories</i> actually had a really cool thaumaturgy ritual for just that scenario, for a good person who's been forced to do or see terrible things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ritual in question:<br /> <br /> <b>River-Washed Memories (3, Intelligence, 5, one night):</b><br /> <br /> This little-known ritual is granted by Luna in her No Moon aspects, particularly the Walker at the Crossroads, to those who cannot live with themselves. It may be employed only at an empty intersection of two paths on a moonless night. Surrounding himself with an unbroken circle of silver, the thaumaturge sits down at the center of the crossroads and meditates on his sins from sundown to sunrise.<br /> <br /> If he is not interrupted during this time, he rises to find that his silver circle has disappeared in the dark of the night, and that he can no longer remember any crimes he committed at any point in his life. (\u201cCrimes\u201d are determined as any action that was illegal in the place where it occurred.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I wouldn't suggest that this alone would be enough to convince Luna to Exalt anyone. There's not enough sacrifice involved.<br /> <br /> When I originally suggested the idea of Luna Choosing someone who inflicted themselves with amnesia, I was thinking of a sort of amnesia that steals away cherished memories as well as painful ones, or that makes the person forget valuable information and skills.<br /> <br /> In order to gain freedom from their past, they need to give up more of it than just the painful parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:50:25-07:00","id":924251,"title":"","content":"Seymour. Seymour is his name. Got mixed up because the cadence of it is so similar to Stanley Kubrick. <br /> <br /> \u200bAlso get the name mixed up with how they pronounce it on Malcolm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:16:10-07:00","id":924417,"title":"","content":"<i>Legend of Zelda:</i> Both the Link of <i>Majora's Mask</i> and the Link of <i>Twilight Princess</i> could be Lunars, and not for the obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> Setting aside his previous adventure (and potential Exaltation moments) in <i>Ocarina of Time</i>, <i>MM</i> Link found himself lost and stranded in an unknown land, and then trapped in an alien body when the Skull Kid uses a curse to transform him into a Deku Scrub child. In this hopeless situation, Link finds the Happy Mask Salesman, who offers to remove the curse if Link promises to find the Skull Kid, take back the Majora's Mask he stole, and return it to the Salesman. But Link not only has to trust that the disturbing and mysterious man can be trusted to uphold his end of the bargain <i>or </i>to not abuse the power of such a Mask for himself, Link first has to prove himself by finding the Skull Kid and managing to take back at least his own Ocarina of Time. Which means risking his life against the Skull Kid.<br /> <br /> But Link decides that the freedom to live in his own body is worth the risk. He hunts down the Skull Kid, reclaims his Ocarina, and then accepts the Happy Mask Salesman's deal to be freed of the curse in return for the promise to steal Majora's Mask and return it to the creepy Salesman.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>TP</i> Link had a similar start. In chasing after the moblins who kidnapped his childhood friend, Link found himself sucked into a strange world, attacked and overpowered by an alien creature, and then for some reason cursed to transform into the body of a wolf; an agonizing experience which causes him to pass out.<br /> <br /> When he awakens, he has no idea where he is or how much time has passed, he is still trapped in the body of a wolf, and further trapped by a manacle chained to the floor within a barred and locked dungeon cell. Freedom of the sort he desires is well and truly beyond his grasp.<br /> <br /> Then an imp appears, and offers him freedom. She breaks his chain, and offers to help him escape if he can figure his own way out of his cell. By exploring his environment and experimenting with his cursed form, he discovers a way to dig his own way out. But then the imp reveals more details about her offer -- she will help Link escape this prison if he agrees to do everything she says.<br /> <br /> Just like <i>MM </i>Link with the Happy Mask Salesman, <i>TP </i>Link is gambling that whatever situation into which he's getting himself isn't worse than the situation he's leaving behind. Out of the frying pan and into the fire, as it were. At the very least, <i>TP </i>Link is betting that he can win his freedom more easily from the imp than he can from the prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T08:53:04-07:00","id":924481,"title":"","content":"For those who have not seen it, the particulars of Little Shop of Horrors that I was alluding to are in this musical number:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://\u200b&#91;url&#93;http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z0kSBiu1IGk&#91;/url&#93;\" target=\"_blank\">https://\u200b&amp;#91;url&amp;#93;http://www.youtube.com...&amp;#91;/url&amp;#93;</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T20:48:45-07:00","id":924758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924217#post924217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, if I extend the concept of chains to be broken to a life situation that, at first blush, is crushingly inescapable...<br /> <br /> \u200bI wonder at the idea of a Seymour Krelboyne who discovers the ravenous monster inside of his own soul rather than in a Chinese-owned shop.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember and read about Seymour, fantastic things just HAPPEN to him. He didn't go looking for a magical monstrous plant from outer space, he just sort of ended up with it. He didn't try escaping from his shitty situation, he just let the monster talk him into murdering some guy based on the fact that the guy was hurting the woman that Seymour liked. Then, in the heat of the moment in which his boss threatened to report him to the police, Seymour tricked him into getting eaten by the monster.<br /> <br /> If Seymour wanted to break his chains, he would have asked that woman out on a date before murdering the dentist. Or at least murderer his boss before the dentist.<br /> <br /> Seymour never stops being a coward, so he never becomes a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=917759#post917759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeling trapped, I kind of like the idea of feeling trapped like an animal and animal instinct taking over for some lunar exaltation...of course I could be totally wrong in my interpretation:<br /> <br /> Gohan SSJ2 transformation vs Cell</div> </div> </div> </div>How is Gohan trapped? If that's an Exaltation moment, it's one marked by the pain of loss and the resolve to murder someone in vengeance. It's not about breaking free from anything, or at least not for the sake of his own freedom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gon's rage over his loss </div> </div> </div>How is Gon trapped?<br /> <br /> You mistake the use of the word &quot;animal&quot;. Just because something can be described as &quot;bestial&quot;, it doesn't suddenly become particularly Lunar.<br /> <br /> Have you forgotten about Solar Limit Breaks like Berserk Anger and Rampaging Avarice? Or about the Resistance Charms called Battle Fury Focus and Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eren transformation </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, Eren was trapped. Arguably, Eren has been trapped his whole life, living behind the walls and wanting to explore the world of the outside wilds.<br /> <br /> While there's not a lot of meaningful actions he could have taken to free himself from inside the titan's stomach, he did at least keep his resolve to fight rather than give in to despair like the poor guy who was swallowed before him. Though we don't know how long that guy might have held out before being <i>boiled alive</i> sapped away his willpower.<br /> <br /> Between that and the monstrous transformation, Eren being treated as Anathema by his own people, and the mysterious society of other transforming monsters like himself outside the walls seeking to destroy Civilization, I'm willing to accept Eren as a Lunar analogue.<br /> <br /> (Mikasa is totally a Dawn Caste)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T21:55:48-07:00","id":924771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924758#post924758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, Eren was trapped. Arguably, Eren has been trapped his whole life, living behind the walls and wanting to explore the world of the outside wilds.<br /> <br /> While there's not a lot of meaningful actions he could have taken to free himself from inside the titan's stomach, he did at least keep his resolve to fight rather than give in to despair like the poor guy who was swallowed before him. Though we don't know how long that guy might have held out before being <i>boiled alive</i> sapped away his willpower.<br /> <br /> Between that and the monstrous transformation, Eren being treated as Anathema by his own people, and the mysterious society of other transforming monsters like himself outside the walls seeking to destroy Civilization, I'm willing to accept Eren as a Lunar analogue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cough injected with a drug by his father cough. Maybe that's just an enabler that might be necessary to get a more literal Lunar-type character in, but it is a bit of a split from the narrative. Speaking of which...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Mikasa is totally a Dawn Caste) </div> </div> </div>Spoilers for later in the manga:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> She and the rest of the Ackerman clan, which includes Levi, have hereditary superhuman potential. So, if she's not a Dragon-Blooded, she's something that propagates heroes in the same manner. Yes, Mikasa ended up Naruto-ed in the end. Her mother might have also had a special inborn familial talent, but I can't recall at the moment.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T22:20:16-07:00","id":924775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924771#post924771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cough injected with a drug by his father cough. Maybe that's just an enabler that might be necessary to get a more literal Lunar-type character in, but it is a bit of a split from the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, if you want to split hairs about sources, then I can rightly point out how almost no one in any story is a Solar Exalt because they're not being blessed with the power of a Sun God. <i>Superman</i> was born with his powers, but no one argues that he's a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Good Hunter is the only character in this thread chosen by a lunar creature, and even that was probably because of his pale blood allowing him to resist the Beast Scourge that comes with the Old Blood, rather than because the thing was impressed by his spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> But Mikasa being a Dragon-Blooded is fine. It still puts her very clearly above the other mortal soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T22:27:43-07:00","id":924777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924775#post924775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, if you want to split hairs about sources, then I can rightly point out how almost no one in any story is a Solar Exalt because they're not being blessed with the power of a Sun God. <i>Superman</i> was born with his powers, but no one argues that he's a Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> The Good Hunter is the only character in this thread chosen by a lunar creature, and even that was probably because of his pale blood allowing him to resist the Beast Scourge that comes with the Old Blood, rather than because the thing was impressed by his spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to go beyond splitting hairs for me. Totems are important, and Eren's titan form is not exactly suggestive of one. It's a giant, misshapen, zombie-like construction that forms around his actual body. This isn't the kind of source where you go more allegorical; it promises monsters right off the bat, and they're a bit of an odd fit for Exalted, since they're giant reverse ch'ih-mei from KotE (empowered by the sun instead of being burned by it) that might eventually turn into someone who can wake up and take control back. This kind of narrative is not really so very Lunar after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T22:46:27-07:00","id":924780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924777#post924777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to go beyond splitting hairs for me. Totems are important, and Eren's titan form is not exactly suggestive of one. It's a giant, misshapen, zombie-like construction that forms around his actual body. This isn't the kind of source where you go more allegorical; it promises monsters right off the bat, and they're a bit of an odd fit for Exalted, since they're giant reverse ch'ih-mei from KotE (empowered by the sun instead of being burned by it) that might eventually turn into someone who can wake up and take control back. This kind of narrative is not really so very Lunar after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if the titans were exchanged for monsters that looked like animals, you wouldn't be complaining, and nothing about the story would be significantly changed, so your objections are rooted in aesthetics rather than themes.<br /> <br /> As I show with Train Heartnet in post 41, I'm willing to focus more on themes than aesthetics, and I'm willing to replace sources like Super Soldier Serums or Radioactive Spider Bites with sources like &quot;the Unconquered Sun / Luna likes you&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T03:06:13-07:00","id":924833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924758#post924758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember and read about Seymour, fantastic things just HAPPEN to him. He didn't go looking for a magical monstrous plant from outer space, he just sort of ended up with it. He didn't try escaping from his shitty situation, he just let the monster talk him into murdering some guy based on the fact that the guy was hurting the woman that Seymour liked. Then, in the heat of the moment in which his boss threatened to report him to the police, Seymour tricked him into getting eaten by the monster.<br /> <br /> If Seymour wanted to break his chains, he would have asked that woman out on a date before murdering the dentist. Or at least murderer his boss before the dentist.<br /> <br /> Seymour never stops being a coward, so he never becomes a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wasn't really thinking about the person, more about the scenario as set up in the Skid Row number; as life in a perennially low income community as a form of confinement that a person could become a Lunar by trying to escape from or overcome it. I feel I could slightly revise Seven Devil Clever's story to fit to that, if she's never directly written up again. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T09:24:45-07:00","id":924908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924833#post924833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI wasn't really thinking about the person, more about the scenario as set up in the Skid Row number; as life in a perennially low income community as a form of confinement that a person could become a Lunar by trying to escape from or overcome it. I feel I could slightly revise Seven Devil Clever's story to fit to that, if she's never directly written up again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.<br /> <br /> I've also considered that Luna might Exalt a daughter who, fighting to free her parents and herself of the web of debts and obligations that snare them, dives into learning the legal code and laws of economics. Especially if the daughter's solution to the Gordian Knot is fraud, blackmail, theft, and/or murder... anything that risks destroying her if she's caught.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although, regarding Seven Devils Clever, one of the things I remember about her is that she Exalted when the Dragon-Blooded lord of her neighborhood was about to kill her to put a stop to her rebellion.<br /> <br /> Maybe she saw him coming and tried to flee for her life, keeping her head about her and using her environment, but after he trapped her anyway, she decided to die free and fighting on her feet instead of surrendering and begging for mercy?<br /> <br /> Though I could see another Lunar Exalting for surrendering and begging for mercy, if the prospective Lunar was always planning to escape captivity at the first opportunity. Less, &quot;I surrender,&quot; and more &quot;<a href=\"https://www.google.de/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiD6o6nl9XNAhWDx4MKHTJRClYQFggeMAA&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Ftvtropes.org%2Fpmwiki%2Fpmwiki.php%2FMain%2FISurrenderSuckers&amp;usg=AFQjCNH73XsrvhKgJEDFs1K4O1glR0Ym1Q\" target=\"_blank\">I surrender, suckers!</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Faithful Pia's Exaltation might need to change. Originally, she was the only survivor of a Guild caravan raid and gang-rape, who found the strength to give her caravan the best burial she could before trying to find her way to water. She was visited by Luna before she was found by Jak the Outrider.<br /> <br /> Simply trying to survive her ordeal could be take as an attempt to win her freedom (from death by deprivation, exposure, and predation), though she could have been kept by her tormentors instead of discarded, and she attempted to escape from them on her own. So she might have Exalted and killed them all before finding her way back to her caravan to bury them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T03:16:38-07:00","id":938010,"title":"","content":"I feel that <i>Resident Evil</i>'s Jill Valentine would be a good 3E Lunar. She begins the third game by springing out a window to escape the zombies after her, and ends it snarling defiance into the maw of a hulking fanged abomination. She survives everything by doing everything- kicking zombies in the face, crafting her own medicine and gunpowder, running through flames to scavenge an anarchic, condemned city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=924908#post924908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply trying to survive her ordeal could be take as an attempt to win her freedom (from death by deprivation, exposure, and predation)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would be boring if <i>every</i> Lunar first exceeded their limits through violence. I want No Moon Hiccup, realizing one day that society's ostracism means nothing to him anymore. I want Full Moon Amba journeying across snowy wilderness- no more hurt by it than the fine palace she was born in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:36:27-07:00","id":938197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938010#post938010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that <i>Resident Evil</i>'s Jill Valentine would be a good 3E Lunar. She begins the third game by springing out a window to escape the zombies after her, and ends it snarling defiance into the maw of a hulking fanged abomination. She survives everything by doing everything- kicking zombies in the face, crafting her own medicine and gunpowder, running through flames to scavenge an anarchic, condemned city.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the emphasis is on freedom rather than survival. How was Jill trapped and how did she try to free herself?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it would be boring if <i>every</i> Lunar first exceeded their limits through violence. </div> </div> </div>Except they are chosen for picking freedom over survival. The only limit is fear, not weakness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I want No Moon Hiccup, realizing one day that society's ostracism means nothing to him anymore. </div> </div> </div>If it doesn't trap him, he doesn't need to free himself from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T08:32:33-07:00","id":938868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938197#post938197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it doesn't trap him, he doesn't need to free himself from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why must escaping always be about death? Breaking metaphysical chains can also be heroic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:04:48-07:00","id":938917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938868#post938868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why must escaping always be about death? Breaking metaphysical chains can also be heroic.</div> </div> </div> </div>People slip out of little entanglements all of the time. What is heroic about them?<br /> <br /> The Sun doesn't make a warrior a Dawn for slaughtering a domesticated chicken for his meal. He Exalts someone willing to fight the most amazing of battles.<br /> <br /> Luna would have similar standards. You have to value freedom more than life itself. Why would she settle for lesser heroes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T10:21:43-07:00","id":938921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938917#post938917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People slip out of little entanglements all of the time. What is heroic about them?<br /> <br /> The Sun doesn't make a warrior a Dawn for slaughtering a domesticated chicken for his meal. He Exalts someone willing to fight the most amazing of battles.<br /> <br /> Luna would have similar standards. You have to value freedom more than life itself. Why would she settle for lesser heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there might be a false dichotomy hear. UCS has exalted people for non-life threatening heroics before, for standing up to him in desperation, for gladitorial matches, and so on. Certainly Luna can recognize the difficulty in trying to escpae social pressures and rebeling against the ties of family and community? The mental wear that does, the level of stress and emotional trouble it brings?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, all Lunars have a sucidial streak or lack a survival instinct. That just...seems off to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:52:16-07:00","id":938989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938917#post938917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna would have similar standards. You have to value freedom more than life itself. Why would she settle for lesser heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because being a lesser hero often signifies one's potential to grow into a greater one. Because opportunities for meaningful, more dramatic acts of heroism are often limited. Because Luna's available talent pool (people who are oppressed/trapped- oppressed by people specifically threatening death- who value potential freedom over concrete things like any family they'd be leaving behind if they died, who are oppressed so egregiously and completely that they're motivated to die fighting it rather than go on living in such a state, who have absolutely nothing of worth in their lives other than the idea of freedom, who also somehow have the opportunity to show this feeling in a big risky stand against their oppressors) is otherwise pretty small. (And lessened even more by the fact that people willing to risk their lives over 'the principle of the thing' tend to be utter maniacs. A Lunar should be the guy who persuaded his village's satrap to lower its unfair tax rates- not the frothing fanatic who attacks that same satrap and gets killed in a meaningless, morale-shattering display of defiance. Heroism is about preserving the good parts of life- or life in general- not just tearing down the bad. Especially when doing the latter might only make things worse by getting everyone else punished for your actions.)<br /> Would it be nice if, say, all the applicants for a robotics job had brought homemade A.I in to let the interviewer judge their skills firsthand? Yes, but in practice that will never happen. So humans invented things like diplomas and references as a cheaper, more portable way of doing the same thing. We have to extrapolate on some level, or the post will never be filled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":476,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","user":"Argonometra","date":". 07-28-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:16:52-07:00","id":939073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938010#post938010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want No Moon Hiccup, realizing one day that society's ostracism means nothing to him anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938917#post938917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People slip out of little entanglements all of the time. What is heroic about them?<br /> <br /> The Sun doesn't make a warrior a Dawn for slaughtering a domesticated chicken for his meal. He Exalts someone willing to fight the most amazing of battles.<br /> <br /> Luna would have similar standards. You have to value freedom more than life itself. Why would she settle for lesser heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Luna would accept someone whose freedom was a change of perspective - whose escape wasn't just in physical form but in mental or social mode as well.<br /> <br /> Let's take someone who is an outsider in or is despised by a community and lives their days chained to the desires of other people, struggling to curry favor and living his life in order to &quot;prove&quot; his worth to that community, only to one day wake up and realize that he didn't <i>need</i> to do it - that the &quot;chains&quot; were simply in his mind all along. As he comes to the realization that he was trapped only because of himself, and he chooses to leave the community to find his own place in the world, I could absolutely see Luna Exalting such a person.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the chains you bind yourself with, the ones constructed in your mind or you are given by a society, are even harder to break than steel handcuffs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T13:54:49-07:00","id":939111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938917#post938917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People slip out of little entanglements all of the time. What is heroic about them?<br /> <br /> The Sun doesn't make a warrior a Dawn for slaughtering a domesticated chicken for his meal. He Exalts someone willing to fight the most amazing of battles.<br /> <br /> Luna would have similar standards. You have to value freedom more than life itself. Why would she settle for lesser heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about being lesser. It's about being bound up in a world view so tightly that you forget the outside boundaries that used to be visible to you. Then along comes a satori, and the rigid, structured world the individual constructed in their own mind - usually with no small amount of help from outside authorities, peer pressure or what have you - comes tumbling down, broken like bars torn out by Star Platinum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:23:01-07:00","id":939245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=938921#post938921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there might be a false dichotomy hear. UCS has exalted people for non-life threatening heroics before, for standing up to him in desperation, for gladitorial matches, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, my words were &quot;[the Sun] Exalts [a Dawn] for being willing to fight the most amazing of battles.&quot;<br /> <br /> The keyword is &quot;willing&quot;. It's not so much that a prospective Dawn must always risk his life to be Chosen, but that he's got the attitude where he would do such a thing. If a Dawn wasn't willing to fight the most amazing battles, then why would the Sun give him the power to do so?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly Luna can recognize the difficulty in trying to escpae social pressures and rebeling against the ties of family and community? </div> </div> </div>You mean running away from your old life to start a new one? Risking your safety and comfort for freedom? Making a big, personal sacrifice? Or at least taking actions that would force you to leave if you're caught and exiled?<br /> <br /> Yes, I think that would impress Luna.<br /> <br /> <br /> Argonometra didn't emphasize anything about what Hiccup's decision would cost him. Argo painted a picture of Hiccup deciding that he didn't care about being the outcast anymore... and that was apparently enough?<br /> <br /> I think if Hiccup catches Luna's eye, it's because Hiccup DOES care about what his people will do if they learn what he's doing, but he keeps doing it ANYWAY. It's because he still cares about his life with them that risking that life has <i>weight</i>. It's because becoming an outcast would hurt him that his decision is courageous.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-28-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T18:36:49-07:00","id":939252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939245#post939245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean running away from your old life to start a new one? Risking your safety and comfort for freedom? Making a big, personal sacrifice? Or at least taking actions that would force you to leave if you're caught and exiled?<br /> <br /> Yes, I think that would impress Luna.<br /> <br /> <br /> Argonometra didn't emphasis anything about what Hiccup's decision would cost him. Argo painted a picture of Hiccup deciding that he didn't care about being the outcast anymore... and that was apparently enough?<br /> <br /> I think if Hiccup catches Luna's eye, it's because Hiccup DOES care about what his people will do if they learn what he's doing, but he keeps doing it ANYWAY. It's because he still cares about his life with them that risking that life has <i>weight</i>. It's because becoming an outcast would hurt him that his decision is courageous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your initial statement lead me to believe you were disqualifying Hiccup for not literally risking immediate physical death. Mea culpa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:02:24-07:00","id":939271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939252#post939252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your initial statement lead me to believe you were disqualifying Hiccup for not literally risking immediate physical death. Mea culpa.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just WILLING to risk death, or at the very least the loss of the life he knows.<br /> <br /> Isn't sacrifice a big part of being Chosen by the gods? People deride Panther's Exaltation story, but at the very least the Sun found Panther in a moment where he was willing to sacrifice everything he had finally achieved in order to have some greater purpose than satisfying his own appetites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T19:13:09-07:00","id":939275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939073#post939073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that Luna would accept someone whose freedom was a change of perspective - whose escape wasn't just in physical form but in mental or social mode as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, accepting a new idea is terrifying because of how it can cast doubt over all other things once held as unshakeable truths.<br /> <br /> I can see Luna falling in love with someone who was not only willing to brave that kind of uncertainty and fear, but willing to follow the Rabbit Hole as deep as it goes in order to learn the real truth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's take someone who is an outsider in or is despised by a community and lives their days chained to the desires of other people, struggling to curry favor and living his life in order to &quot;prove&quot; his worth to that community, only to one day wake up and realize that he didn't <i>need</i> to do it - that the &quot;chains&quot; were simply in his mind all along. As he comes to the realization that he was trapped only because of himself, and he chooses to leave the community to find his own place in the world, I could absolutely see Luna Exalting such a person.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the chains you bind yourself with, the ones constructed in your mind or you are given by a society, are even harder to break than steel handcuffs. </div> </div> </div>But action must follow resolution.<br /> <br /> The woman who leapt into shark infested waters realized what she needed to do to be free, but Luna only Chose her after the mortal committed herself to her course.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the man who decides that he will no longer live like a slave must change how he lives... which should not be easy, because that is the only way he knows how to live. It is familiar, and therefore comfortable, second-nature, the path of least resistance when his strength fails him.<br /> <br /> I think Luna would Exalt a drunkard who beats his addiction in order to free himself from the tyranny of booze or drugs. But he needs to ACT, and the path is not easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T21:04:06-07:00","id":939321,"title":"","content":"&quot;Action&quot; was never a requirement for Exaltation in past editions, whether as a Solar, Lunar or Dragon Blooded and I am uncertain if it is mandatory in this edition. Of course, I admit that I'm not even really sure what you mean by &quot;action&quot; in the first place. After Exalting most Exalted do undertake various actions to change the world around them. In fact, I can't think of a single one who <i>hasn't</i> tried changing something about the world and their place in it after Exaltation, even if it's just using their powers to do the exact same things they used to do only better.<br /> <br /> In other words, I think action is a very natural consequence of Exaltation and the change in perspective, power and magical abilities it brings rather than a requirement.<br /> <br /> In my mind the most important thing for a would-be Lunar is the decision to break free from their chains, even if they don't have any other goal or desire in mind at that time. What they choose to do afterwards isn't as important the initial chain breaking - that's what attracts Luna's attention to them.<br /> <br /> Oftentimes decision is coupled with action, such as the woman who leaps into a pool of sharks to escape slavery. Certainly among Solars I would guess that the number who Exalted &quot;while taking action&quot; exceeds the number who didn't. I also accept that Luna and the Sun may have different standards for Exaltation. Still, I think simply recognizing that there <i>are</i> no chains on you, that the only person keeping you chained is yourself and casting those chains off can be just as worthy of Luna's attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T23:10:22-07:00","id":939371,"title":"","content":"The confusing thing about spiritual/intellectual achievements is that the effort put into achieving them is difficult to quantify. Ragara Jasir Exalted while meditating on the Imperial Mountain; Ragara Bhagwei Exalted in a moment of metaphysical epiphany, only inventing a cure <i>after</i> that; Arianna Exalted while analyzing a text, in defiance of her peers' sexism. When do thoughts become as important as physical/quantifiable actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T17:46:59-07:00","id":960764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939321#post939321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Action&quot; was never a requirement for Exaltation in past editions, whether as a Solar, Lunar or Dragon Blooded and I am uncertain if it is mandatory in this edition. Of course, I admit that I'm not even really sure what you mean by &quot;action&quot; in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for taking so long.<br /> <br /> You remember my posts earlier in this thread about why I don't think Morgiana would be Exalted as a Lunar? She clearly hates both periods of her slavery, but she never attempts to free herself. Even when she finally does free herself, it's not about herself, it's just to save someone else who is being publicly executed in front of her. But she could have tried escaping with that little girl earlier, before the girl was to be put to death.<br /> <br /> Maybe I was being too dismissive, but I'm really wary of characters who make noises about wanting freedom without ever actually having the conviction to risk their lives for it, and the surest way to know that someone would rather die than remain trapped is to actively do something that could get them killed.<br /> <br /> <br /> But while I'm dredging the thread back up, how about another example of a possible Lunar?<br /> <br /> Kratos, from the <i>God of War</i> series. After Ares tricks him into murdering his own wife and daughter -- apparently the only human beings in the world that this sociopath cared about -- Kratos was plagued with terrible guilt and nightmares. He refused to allow himself any sense of peace, and ultimately struck a deal with Athena to kill the god of war in return for peace.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could see Kratos' inability to escape his nightmares and guilt as his own fault. It <i>is</i> something he's doing to himself, on some level, because he refuses to face his actions, accept them, and move on. And even though he chooses to commit suicide rather than suffer any more, it's still running away from his problems instead of facing them.<br /> <br /> So, maybe he's not as fitting as Shark Lady, after all? I mean, when <i>she </i>jumped into shark-infested waters, it was to run away from a situation being imposed upon her rather than an internal issue could try to resolve herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T18:39:43-07:00","id":960784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939371#post939371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The confusing thing about spiritual/intellectual achievements is that the effort put into achieving them is difficult to quantify. Ragara Jasir Exalted while meditating on the Imperial Mountain; Ragara Bhagwei Exalted in a moment of metaphysical epiphany, only inventing a cure <i>after</i> that; Arianna Exalted while analyzing a text, in defiance of her peers' sexism. When do thoughts become as important as physical/quantifiable actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>The completion of a project that feels like an albatross hanging from your neck? Quite possibly one that's an unpleasant requirement of something you actually wanted to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:36:09-07:00","id":960833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=960764#post960764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I was being too dismissive, but I'm really wary of characters who make noises about wanting freedom without ever actually having the conviction to risk their lives for it, and the surest way to know that someone would rather die than remain trapped is to actively do something that could get them killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, in the end, it's important to remember that Lunar Exaltation isn't a computerized process with a &quot;Yes&quot; and &quot;No&quot; switch. Rather, Luna chooses who Exalts and she has a subjective opinion on who deserves her blessing and why. While, for the most part, she is going to choose people who are seeking to free themselves, there might be times where she doesn't. I think it's reasonable that she may view someone who wants to escape from bondage and has considered doing so, but just doesn't quite have enough courage to do it, so she provides him with Exalted to finally find his own freedom.<br /> <br /> I don't want to say that Luna is fickle, but at the same time I don't think that all Lunars are going to cleave to a specific mold. I feel that it's fine if you have a broad concept for who Exalts as a Lunar (people seeking freedom), but a fair amount of fuzziness when you start looking at the exact details.<br /> <br /> I don't think players will have to worry about presenting their character and being told, &quot;Sorry, but your character wasn't <i>seeking</i> freedom,&quot; or, &quot;Sorry, but your character wasn't seeking freedom in the <i>right</i> way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T09:16:23-07:00","id":961081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=939271#post939271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, just WILLING to risk death, or at the very least the loss of the life he knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all characters- especially those who know anything abut Creation's cosmology- will see death as freeing. Is life the only thing worth sacrificing, the only coin that can 'buy' Luna's respect? (Must every Lunar be escaping society specifically and sticking it to the man? Because that sounds too much like 1E to me.) Why aren't internal reformists or innovative, say, architects, just as much Lunar as tough mohawked rebels with a cause?<br /> <br /> Honestly, I couldn't take seriously a backstory where some No Moon Roark-expy stakes his life on how a roof should be designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:48:07-07:00","id":961253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/917135-lunars-characters-from-other-media-who-felt-trapped?p=961081#post961081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all characters- especially those who know anything abut Creation's cosmology- will see death as freeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the corebook makes it clear that all LUNARS were chosen because they valued freedom more than life.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that all of them tried to commit suicide, but it DOES mean that all of them were at least willing to risk their lives. They were willing to risk SOMETHING important to themselves, anyway.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, as you yourself quoted me saying, that means risking the loss &quot;of the life he knows&quot;. His livelihood, family, status, wealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is life the only thing worth sacrificing, the only coin that can 'buy' Luna's respect? </div> </div> </div>Creation has a LOT of people to choose from. If Luna wanted, she could surely be picky enough to Choose only 400 people out of everyone in Creation who risks their lives for freedom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Must every Lunar be escaping society specifically and sticking it to the man? Because that sounds too much like 1E to me. </div> </div> </div>Why do you think society and The Man are the only forms of slavery and entrapment in the world?<br /> <br /> I've given other examples. Bloodborne's Good Hunter was trapped within his own sickly body. Two different Links were trapped under polymorphic curses. Kratos agreed to perform legendary feats for Athena in return for freedom from his own nightmares.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why aren't internal reformists or innovative, say, architects, just as much Lunar as tough mohawked rebels with a cause? </div> </div> </div>What do those paths have to do with personal freedom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}